course: dictionary
lesson: 15412
title: A wheel with teeth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. These words are its context, and they give clues. «The chain slipped off the sprocket, so the pedals spun but the back wheel stayed still.» The chain has to sit on something to make the wheel turn, so a sprocket must be a toothed wheel that the chain fits onto.
explain: «The big front sprocket and the small back sprocket made the back wheel spin faster.» Two wheels of different sizes work together, so a sprocket is one of the toothed wheels that the chain goes round. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Sprockets are used in other places too. «The camera pulled the film along by the little holes in its edge.» Those holes are called sprocket holes, because the toothed wheel fits into them and turns the film. In each case a sprocket has teeth that fit into something, and that is how it turns or is turned.
fact: A sprocket is a wheel with teeth around its edge.
fact: The teeth fit into the links of a chain, or into the holes in a film or tape.
fact: On a bicycle, the toothed wheels the chain goes round are sprockets.
fact: A big front sprocket and a small back sprocket can make the back wheel turn faster.
fact: Sprocket holes are the holes in the edge of film, which the toothed wheel fits into.
exercise: «The chain slipped off the sprocket, so the pedals spun but the wheel stayed still.» What is a sprocket? | A brake that stops the bike | *A wheel with teeth that fit into a chain | A small bell on the handlebars | A seat for the rider
exercise: «Ravi counted the teeth on the small back sprocket.» Where would you find a sprocket? | Inside a loaf of bread | At the bottom of a pond | Up in the sky | *On a bicycle, where the chain goes round
exercise: Mia says sprockets are like gears. What do sprockets pass from one wheel to another? | Sound | Colour | *Turning force | Water
test: «The front sprocket is big, and the back sprocket is small.» Which sprocket makes the back wheel turn faster? | Neither, because the chain does it alone | *The small back sprocket | Both are the same size, so neither one | The big front sprocket
test: «The old film had little holes along its edge.» What are those holes called? | Chain links | Spoke holes | *Sprocket holes | Gear teeth
exam: «The rear sprocket and the chain turned together.» What does a sprocket do with a chain? | It cuts the chain in two | It paints the chain a new colour | *It turns the chain, or is turned by it | It makes the chain louder
